\subsection*{A12. Why only KPI reconstruction during pretraining?}

\reviewcomment{
Why is pretraining limited to masked time-series reconstruction?
Did you consider reconstruction of tabular features or contrastive
objectives?
}

\response{
Our pretraining objective is designed to learn reusable representations
of RAN operational behavior. KPI time series directly reflect the
dynamic network behavior resulting from RAN properties and operating
conditions. Configuration parameters, in contrast, are largely
operator-defined settings and do not exhibit the same natural temporal
dynamics. We therefore use KPI reconstruction to align the
self-supervised objective with the behavior-modeling goal of RAN-NFM.

