\subsection*{C2. Control-theoretic and DRL baselines}

\reviewcomment{
The evaluation does not compare against other classes of RAN management
methods, such as control-theoretic solutions or deep-RL-based RAN
optimization.
}

\response{
These approaches generally solve specific closed-loop control or
optimization problems, whereas RAN-NFM focuses on learning reusable
representations for RAN behavior prediction that can be adapted to
different downstream tasks. A direct comparison would therefore require
aligning the task objectives, action spaces, and control interfaces.

We agree that using the learned RAN-NFM representation within
control- or RL-based decision systems is an interesting future
direction, but we do not claim experimental superiority over these
systems in the current work.
}

